    "source": "From the 9 October school update: copying and continuing simple patterns, creating them and spotting them in a story.",
    "everyday": [
      "<b>Autumn treasure:</b> conkers, acorns, pine cones in a line: conker, acorn, conker, acorn. School wants these brought in too.",
      "<b>Clothes:</b> stripes on socks, pyjamas, jumpers. \"What colour comes next?\"",
      "<b>Setting the table:</b> fork, spoon, fork, spoon.",
      "<b>Body patterns:</b> clap, stomp, clap, stomp. Then your child makes one for you to copy.",
      "<b>Bear Hunt:</b> the repeated lines are a pattern in words. Which bit repeats, which bit changes?",
      "<b>Out and about:</b> railings, paving, tiles, zebra crossings."
    ],
